+- OBJ import works, but OBJ export is not reachable through `Scene.save()`, for two independent
+  reasons reproduced directly against this build: `ObjExporter._write_obj()` builds its content
+  as a Python `str` and writes it straight to the stream `Scene.save()` always opens in binary
+  mode, which raises `TypeError: a bytes-like object is required, not 'str'`; and, separately,
+  calling `ObjExporter.export()` directly with a correctly-typed text stream still writes zero
+  bytes, because `_collect_nodes()` only inspects the node it is first called with and descends
+  into child nodes from inside that same check — so it finds nothing whenever the scene's
+  entities live on named child nodes, which is how every example in this README builds a scene.
+  No test in this repository exercises OBJ export.
